Edition No. 44 — Sunday, 15 November 2026

9 stories: Three petitions and no sponsor: Mwiimbu says the government will not interfere with calls to remove term limits, and will not say whether Hichilema would sign one (lead); 'How can we be unpopular?': in Choma, Hichilema points to 14 by-election wins, promises a dual carriageway to the south and says FRA money will arrive within 10 to 15 days; Two per cent of everything: Cabinet moves the NHIMA deduction from basic to gross pay from January 2027, as the Treasury takes on the scheme's K1.7 billion debt and dialysis bill; The raid video stays, two paragraphs go: the High Court splits the DPP's objection in the Mundubile and Zulu bail case, and a defence lawyer says three of the 18 could walk; The court goes to the patient: Judge Mulenga visits Jay Jay Banda at Maina Soko after a surgeon's report of a shattered shinbone, with the habeas corpus ruling still to come; £3 billion in and more promised: at the King's birthday reception Britain's envoy pledges investment for Grow Zambia, and the mines minister asks for help towards 3 million tonnes; Chilufya scores, Girumugisha answers, Algeria pull three clear: a 1–1 draw before 44,000 in Ndola leaves Zambia second in Group I, with the return in Bujumbura on Tuesday; Two clear goals or out: the under-23s host Burkina Faso at Heroes at 15:00 today, Patrick Chinyemba's professional debut ends in defeat, and Sporting Lusaka lift the Roberts Cup; No visa, no Puerto Rico: Zambia withdraws from the 75th Miss Universe after its nurse-contestant is caught by US travel restrictions, with Congo out too and Zimbabwe still waiting.

